# .mailmap — canonical identities for git log / blame / contributors display.
#
# Syntax (see `man gitmailmap`):
#   Proper Name <proper-email> Commit Name <commit-email>
#
# Only the display changes — the underlying commit metadata is untouched.
# GitHub honours this file for the Contributors graph, commit lists, and
# `git shortlog` output.  That lets us attribute every commit to a single
# human without rewriting history or force-pushing.

# The `claude/*` branch workflow authored commits as "Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>".
# Collapse them under the repo owner's canonical identity.
Trustydev212 <Trustyboi212@gmail.com> Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
